MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Combat can destroy population-providing structures while units live,
opening a temporary over-cap window. The classic RTS rule — usage may
exceed cap; new spawns block at the gate until headroom returns — is
adopted here as M6's first work item (the brief calls this out as
blocking honest combat).

The A12 `population <= cap` invariant is therefore relaxed to a
cap-non-corrupt + usage-non-saturating assertion. The M5 production
queue already holds completed items at the queue front when headroom
is missing (A-042), so the spawn side is already the gate — no
production-semantics change. §9.4's reading is untouched.

- A-049 superseded by A-053 (audit-trail strike-through kept).
- DEBT-010 retired.
- The strict-over-cap should_panic test is replaced by
  `population_drift_far_past_cap_fires`, which pins the wild-drift
  catch-all (saturating usage far above cap is still a bookkeeping bug).
---
