From 5ab8307289377554859b0863ffa2d5634b239904 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: M6 Agent <m6@pandemonium.local>
Date: Sat, 3 Oct 2026 10:57:39 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 02/12] feat(sim): map Attack capability at the world seam
 (DEBT-006 retired)
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

The Attack capability is the last carried-but-unmapped capability
(DEBT-006). It now flows the full data path: bundle seam → CapTemplate
→ CapabilityData → runtime AttackDef → state hash (slot 11, encoding v4).

Sim side (crates/sim/):
- world.rs: AttackDef (damage, range, cooldown_ticks, cooldown_remaining,
  acquire_range, target) + CapabilityData::Attack variant + attack store
  + attack_of/_mut accessors + has_attack() + spawn/remove arms.
- world.rs: Order::AttackUnit { target: EntityId } — a commanded attack
  on a specific entity. The combat pipeline pops it on target death.
- fixture.rs: CapTemplate::Attack { damage, range_milli_tiles,
  cooldown_ms, acquire_range_milli_tiles } + encode arm (tag 11) +
  to_runtime arm (ms → ticks via the shared ms_to_ticks).
- hash.rs: STATE_ENCODING_VERSION 3 → 4; bit 11 of the capability mask;
  slot 11 of capability_of; per-entity Attack block (damage, range,
  cooldown_ticks, cooldown_remaining, acquire_range, target tag +
  EntityId); encode_order arm for Order::AttackUnit (tag 4).
- invariants.rs: attack store added to the A12 ascending-id check.
- economy.rs: travel_target returns None for AttackUnit (combat owns
  its chase; movement_target resolves the target's current position).
- movement.rs: movement_target resolves AttackUnit to the target's
  current pos (chase — path rebuilds when it completes so a fleeing
  target is followed); consume_waypoint no longer pops AttackUnit on
  path completion (combat pops it on target death); crowded arrival
  never pops AttackUnit (the attacker keeps chasing).

Content side (crates/content/):
- bundle.rs: capability_template's Attack arm flips None → Some, mapping
  all four Attack fields into CapTemplate::Attack. The content encoder
  already includes Attack data (encode_capability tag 3), so the
  content hash is unchanged — only what the simulation sees changes.
- bundle.rs: doc comment on world() updated (Attack no longer "remains
  validated-and-carried").

Tests (tests/):
- determinism.rs: golden hashes regenerated for encoding v4 (the M6
  encoding bump's review-visible signal, mirroring A-050's pattern).

Encoding notes:
- STATE_ENCODING_VERSION: 3 → 4.
- FIXTURE_ENCODING_VERSION: 3 → 4 (Attack CapTemplate is a new variant).
- Tools headless demo's final hash moved from 0xbc86a622e357252d to
  0x9d5ba9b565060336 (seed 7, 300 ticks) — intentional, see A-056.
- content-validate's content hash unchanged (0x249b69f0ee343a10) — the
  seam flip is invisible to the bundle identity by construction.

Combat pipeline (stage 7) and Attack command semantics (gate) arrive in
the next commits — this one only wires the data path.
