Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

A new `crates/sim/src/combat.rs` module implements the M6 attack
pipeline per plan §9.2 — every stage a named function so future armor,
projectiles, and abilities insert at a stage:

  1. acquire      — pick a target (commanded > units-attacking-friendly >
                    other units > structures); ties to lower id (A-057)
  2. validate     — target alive, in range (squared-distance compare)
  3. wind_up      — 0 ticks in Alpha (placeholder stage)
  4. hit          — damage applied this tick if cooldown allows + in range
  5. mitigate     — identity in Alpha (future armor / reduction)
  6. apply        — subtract from Health.hp, saturating at 0
  7. death        — handled by stage 8 (advance_health_and_cleanup),
                    already wired — combat only mutates hp
  8. credit       — carried on AttackHit's `attacker` field; future kill
                    counts / XP insert here

Wiring:
- lib.rs: `mod combat` + pub re-export of `AttackDef`.
- sim.rs: stage 7 calls `combat::advance_combat(&mut self.world, &mut
  self.events)`; stage 8 calls `combat::clear_dead_targets` after the
  removal pass so attacker target slots pointing at the dead don't
  dangle (ids are never reused, so a stale slot would never re-resolve).

Determinism invariants (plan §5):
- Attackers iterate ascending EntityId (the store's invariant).
- Targets scanned ascending id; ties to lower id.
- All distance tests are squared-distance comparisons — no roots.
- Damage is integer; cooldown is in whole ticks.
- Collect-then-mutate: pending hits + per-attacker updates queued,
  applied after the acquisition pass releases its borrows.

Per-attacker runtime state (`AttackDef::cooldown_remaining` and
`target`) is persisted through a dedicated pass — `tick_cooldown`
runs at step 0 (before any decision), and the acquisition pass writes
its decisions back through `persist(...)`. The cooldown semantics:
cooldown_ticks=N means the attacker hits every Nth tick after the first.

7 new combat unit tests cover: hp reduction + AttackHit event, cooldown
blocking, multi-tick cooldown cadence, out-of-range behavior (acquire
but don't hit), auto-acquisition picking the closest enemy unit, dead-
target slot clearing, and mitigate-identity.

Encoding unchanged (v4) — combat state lives in the AttackDef block
already added in the previous commit. Tools headless hash unchanged.
