An end-to-end Sim test that drives an attacker through two hits (tick 0
+ tick 1) into a target whose hp reaches zero, then verifies the death
lifecycle per plan §9.2 stage 8:

- The target's hp 0 → Event::Died fires the same tick.
- The target is removed the same tick (entities.len() drops from 2 to 1).
- The id is never reused: next_entity_id is 3, not 2.
- Stage 8's combat::clear_dead_targets drops the attacker's target slot
  (verified via a new Sim::attack_probe test-only accessor — the same
  shape as the existing order_probe/lifecycle_probe/queue_probe).
- A follow-up Attack command on the dead id 2 is rejected by the gate
  as InvalidTarget (check_target returns InvalidTarget when the entity
  is absent — ids are never reused, so the dead id stays absent).

The fixture: a 16x16 fully-passable world with two players. Attacker
kind (damage 15, range 1 tile, cooldown_ms 33 → 1 tick), target kind
(30 hp). The attacker acquires + hits on tick 0 (hp 30 → 15, cooldown
set to 1), tick_cooldown decrements to 0 at tick 1's start, ready →
hit → target hp 0 → Died.

A-045 stays carried-forward as-is: a construction site whose builder
dies stalls. The brief flagged it as 'decide A-045 if M6 makes dead
builders common' — M6's combat kills units but a builder's death is
still a corner case (builders are typically workers behind the lines,
not on the front). DEBT.md A-045 entry unchanged.
