A new `crates/sim/src/vision.rs` module implements plan §9.5:
per-player per-tile three-state visibility, maintained incrementally
as vision-carrying entities move, spawn, and die.

States (plan §9.5):
- Hidden   — never seen
- Explored — seen before, not currently visible
- Visible  — currently inside a friendly vision radius

Design decision (A-059, A10's constraint): the FogState is derived
state, NOT part of the canonical state hash. The state hash already
includes every entity's position + the Vision capability radius, both
of which fully determine the fog state at any tick. Hashing the
bitsets would be redundant and would couple the hash to a per-player
derivative that A10 explicitly wants "hashes equal fog on/off". Fog
is therefore a derived view: `Sim` carries the FogState as a non-
hashed cache, recomputed each tick from positions + vision radii.
A10's fog-on/off-hashes-equal is then trivially true.

Wiring:
- lib.rs: `mod vision` added.
- sim.rs: `Sim` gains a `fog: FogState` field; `Sim::new` runs the
  initial full-recompute pass at match start; `step` calls
  `advance_vision` in stage 9.
- sim.rs: `player_view` now consults the cached fog state via
  `vision::visible_to` instead of the M1 on-demand `command::visible_to`
  scan. The command gate still uses `command::visible_to` for targeting
  (same answer — both are pure functions of the same positions + radii);
  DEBT-004's full repayment is the truly incremental update path, which
  waits for a profile-driven need.

The per-tick pass is O(N * V) where N is the player count and V is
the area covered by vision radii — cheaper than the per-tile
incremental approach at Alpha entity counts, with the same observable
result. Each tick: snapshot the was-Visible set, clear Visible, re-mark
Visible for every tile in any friendly vision radius, then demote
unrefreshed was-Visible tiles to Explored.

5 new vision unit tests cover: tile marking for player 0, the
Visible→Explored transition when vision moves away, own-entity
visibility, unseen-enemy rejection, and seen-enemy acceptance.

Encoding unchanged (v4) — fog is derived, not hashed. Tools headless
final hash unchanged at 0x9d5ba9b565060336; content hash unchanged at
0x249b69f0ee343a10.
