Two new acceptance test files (tests/combat.rs and tests/vision.rs)
plus A12 combat invariants in the checker.

tests/combat.rs (7 tests):
- composition_matters_ranged_vs_melee — 3 riflemen vs 3 raiders, AttackMove
  toward center, AttackHit + Died events fire, bit-identical run-to-run.
- composition_change_produces_different_hash — rifle-vs-rifle vs melee-vs-
  melee on the same ground, same script, 5 ticks: hashes differ (composition
  changes the outcome).
- position_matters_two_sided_vs_one_sided — same composition, two-sided
  vs one-sided attack: hashes differ (position changes the outcome).
- combat_skirmish_is_bit_identical_run_to_run — A1 applied to combat.
- turret_attacks_but_does_not_move — a Turret (no Move, Attack+Footprint)
  auto-acquires and fires at an approaching raider; the turret's position
  is unchanged across ticks (no Move capability).
- a12_combat_invariants_hold_every_tick_in_debug — a combat soak: running
  the test in debug IS the soak (the A12 checker fires inside every step).
- legibility_attackhit_and_died_events_fire — the machine-verifiable half
  of the legibility checklist; the human eyeball pass rides DEBT-008.

tests/vision.rs (5 tests):
- a10_fog_integrity_hashes_equal_observer_vs_player_view — the canonical
  state hash is identical whether the observer asks for the full snapshot
  (no fog) or a player_view (fog-filtered). A-059 makes this trivially
  true: fog is derived, not hashed.
- a10_targeting_rejects_unseen_target — Attack on a non-visible target
  is rejected as NotVisible (one direction of the targeting test).
- a10_targeting_accepts_seen_target — Attack on a visible target lands
  and fires AttackHit (the other direction).
- three_state_transition_hidden_to_visible — a tile the player has never
  seen is Hidden; once a friendly unit moves within vision, the enemy
  appears in player_view (the Visible → Explored transition is exercised
  by the unit test in crates/sim/src/vision.rs).
- fd8_hidden_entities_behave_identically — two runs with player 0's
  watcher at different positions; player 1's watcher behaves identically
  (same position, same hp) in both runs. Fog filters the view, not the
  simulation.

A12 combat invariants (crates/sim/src/invariants.rs):
- cooldown_remaining <= cooldown_ticks (never negative; the tick_cooldown
  floor + consume reset keep it bounded).
- An attacker's target slot must point at a live entity (stage 8's
  clear_dead_targets drops slots pointing at the dead — a stale slot
  would never resolve since ids are never reused).
- Targeting your own entity is forbidden at the gate (InvalidTarget), so
  the runtime slot can never hold a friendly id either.

Encoding unchanged (v4). Headless hash unchanged (0x9d5ba9b565060336);
content hash unchanged (0x249b69f0ee343a10). 269 tests passing (was 244
at M5 baseline; +25 M6 tests: 8 combat unit + 5 vision unit + 7 combat
acceptance + 5 vision acceptance).
